abstract: >-
  Design documentation, firmware and test reports for a 12 V LiFePO₄ DC
  uninterruptible power supply that keeps a Home Assistant host (ASRock
  N100DC-ITX, on an 18 V boost rail) and an Xfinity XB7 cable modem running
  through grid outages. A Mean Well HDR-60-12 floats the pack through a
  MOSFET ideal diode, a Victron BP-65 provides the low-voltage disconnect,
  and an ESPHome INA260 monitor on a custom carrier PCB coulomb-counts each
  outage and drives Home Assistant's graceful host shutdown. Includes the
  bill of materials, wiring, FMEA, the original design set, dated discharge
  test reports with raw data, and a planned bench top-off charger.
